error[NK2107]: You're changing `names` in an `async` task, and `names` is bound outside it.
  --> tests/async_outer_write_a_push.nika:4:2
   |
 4 | 	async fn { names.push("a") }
   |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A task runs at the same time as everything after its start, so it would write `names` while the rest of the program reads or writes it.
   = help: Have the task produce a value, `let n = async count()`, and use it after, or keep `names` in a `SharedMut` and change it through `update`.
1 name changed from code that runs at the same time as other code
